WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Choose a workspace and environment. Open Dev Tools > API keys. This walkthrough uses only the fictional demo workspace.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Name the key and set its lifetime. The key stays in this workspace and environment. Choose an expiry between 1 and 365 days.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Choose the access your integration needs. Read-only, product-specific and billing profiles serve different purposes. The guide below lists every permission.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
All products covers Insights and Signal. This profile includes both products and shared API operations. Billing access is separate.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Sandbox testing is for complete test journeys. Owners can use this Sandbox-only profile for product scenarios and simulated billing.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Confirm identity when creating a key. This demonstration cancels the form. No secret is created or displayed.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Inspect the saved key record. Review scopes, expiry and environment in its drawer. Keep actual key secrets in your server secret manager.
